# LINE ENDINGS ARE PART OF THE BUILD OUTPUT HERE, NOT A PREFERENCE.
#
# vercel.json carries a SHA-256 of the inline <script> exactly as it ships. On a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true the working copy is CRLF, so build.mjs
# would hash CRLF text — while git stores, and Vercel serves, LF. The committed
# hash would then describe a file that does not exist anywhere, the browser
# would refuse the script, and the site would be blank in production while every
# local check passed.
#
# build.mjs also normalises its inputs, so this is the second of two defences
# rather than the only one. Both are cheap; neither alone is comfortable.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
